From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:13:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Disable the USB-C ports for
 now

The device tree on this branch enables three blocks for the first time
on the 14-inch MacBook Pro (M4, 2024): PCIe port 0 with its DART, the
two USB-C ports with their SPMI port controllers, and the AOP audio
group. With it the machine hangs early in boot: the boot logo stays up
and nothing is printed, both with this kernel and with an older one
(MEASURED 2026-11-04). The same device tree with these three blocks
disabled, and nothing else changed, boots with this kernel (MEASURED
2026-11-04).

Which of the three blocks causes the hang, alone or only in
combination, is not known yet (root cause TO-VERIFY). Disable both ATC
PHYs, both DWC3 controllers, their four DARTs and SPMI bus A0, which
carries only the two SN201202X port controllers (usb-pd@a and
usb-pd@c) in this tree, until a J604 boot with them enabled has been
shown to work. Only the status lines change, so enabling them again is
a revert of this change.

The internal keyboard and trackpad (MTP) do not depend on any of these
nodes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 23 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index ccb3210c3b..9b27f48a60 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -280,10 +280,15 @@
  * tree), USB2 only. Their SN201202X port controllers sit on SPMI A0; the
  * third controller on that bus (hpm5, USID 8) is the MagSafe port and is
  * not described.
+ *
+ * Disabled for now, with the SPMI bus of the port controllers: a J604 device
+ * tree that enables these ports together with PCIe and the AOP hangs early
+ * boot, before the console. Enable them again once a J604 boot with them
+ * enabled has been shown to work.
  */
 
 &nub_spmi_a0 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-SPMIA0-1, DTV-SPMIA0-2 */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-SPMIA0-1, DTV-SPMIA0-2 */
 
 	hpm1: usb-pd@a {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-sn201202x", "apple,sn201202x";
@@ -357,7 +362,7 @@
 };
 
 &atcphy0 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-0a */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-0a */
 
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -373,16 +378,16 @@
 };
 
 &dwc3_0_dart_0 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-0c */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-0c */
 };
 
 &dwc3_0_dart_1 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-0c */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-0c */
 };
 
 &dwc3_0 {
 	dr_mode = "host";
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-0b */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-0b */
 
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -398,7 +403,7 @@
 };
 
 &atcphy1 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1a */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-1a */
 
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -414,16 +419,16 @@
 };
 
 &dwc3_1_dart_0 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1c */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-1c */
 };
 
 &dwc3_1_dart_1 {
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1c */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-1c */
 };
 
 &dwc3_1 {
 	dr_mode = "host";
-	status = "okay"; /* DTV-USB-1b */
+	status = "disabled"; /* DTV-USB-1b */
 
 	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
